</section>

<section class="architecture-study" aria-labelledby="study-title">
  <div class="page-shell study-layout">
    <div class="study-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">One project · one architecture</p>
      <h2 id="study-title">RepoPact records stay authoritative in RepoPact's documented model.</h2>
      <p>The CLI and Workbench read governed records and request supported operations from Core. The engine validates records and prepares plans. Dashboards and graph views are derived surfaces, while evidence records observed results.</p>
      <p>This diagram documents RepoPact Core. It does not describe ForgeWire, Fabric, Anvil, Flink, or a shared ForgeWire Labs platform.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core/blob/614689b127cf52f801877cc48440f7e45c3709eb/docs/assets/readme/repopact-architecture.svg">Open the source diagram <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <figure class="architecture-figure architecture-figure--large">
      <img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg" alt="RepoPact Core architecture: people and client applications interact with the canonical Rust engine; repository records remain authoritative; evidence and derived views record observed or computed information." aria-describedby="engineering-diagram-notes" width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>Architecture copied from RepoPact Core's public documentation. <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg">Open the full-size diagram</a>.</figcaption>
      <p class="diagram-notes" id="engineering-diagram-notes"><strong>Diagram key.</strong> Blue arrows mark exchanges with Core. Slate arrows mark human or host interactions, evidence, and derived-view relationships. Dashed boxes are derived views; the host/CI integration is optional and provider-specific.</p>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

